        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this superb 1-bedroom ground floor apartment to the market, ideally positioned within the beautifully maintained Hybreasal House development on South Circular Road, Kilmainham, Dublin 8.\n\nNo. 81 Hybreasal House is a bright and spacious 1-bedroom, 1-bathroom apartment presented in turn-key condition throughout. This attractive property comes to the market vacant with no onward chain, offering an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike.\n\nThe well-proportioned internal accommodation comprises an inviting entrance hallway, a generous open-plan living and dining area, a fully fitted kitchen, a spacious double bedroom with fitted storage, and a main bathroom. The property has been exceptionally well maintained and is ready for immediate occupation.\n\nFurther benefits include one designated parking space, excellent storage, and a highly sought-after location within a mature and well-kept residential development. Situated in the heart of Kilmainham, residents can enjoy a wealth of local amenities including cafés, restaurants, shops, parks and excellent transport links, all within easy reach of Dublin City Centre.\n\nSure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers, this fantastic apartment is expected to generate significant interest. Early viewing is highly advised please contact RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today to arrange a viewing.\n\n________________________________________\nFeatures\n• 1 bed / 1 bath\n• C. 58 sqm of internal floorspace\n• BER C\n• Coming to market vacant with no chain\n• Beautifully maintained development\n• One designated parking space \n• Bright and spacious accommodation\n• Management fees c. 2700 per annum\n• Highly sought-after Kilmainham location\n• Walking distance to a host of local amenities\n• Excellent transport links nearby\n• Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers and investors\n• Early viewing strongly advised\n\nDirections \nEircode - D08 AXC8\n"
